Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the component authoring conventions. Here's the complete breakdown:

## 1. **Button Component Record Structure**

[Button record](formats/components/src/components/button/index.ts):

```ts
import { defineComponent, type Definition } from "../../lib/define.ts";
import { css } from "../../lib/css.ts";
import { AI_ICON_MASK } from "../../lib/helpers.ts";
import { SENTINEL } from "../../lib/sentinel.ts";
import { appendGenerated } from "../../lib/aliases.ts";
import { button as buttonRaw } from "../../generated/component-styles.ts";

const interpolatedRules = (p: string) =>
  // prettier-ignore
  css`
/* The ai glyph, added automatically to every AI button and painted in its own colour. */
.${p}button.-color-ai::before,
.${p}button.-color-ai-secondary::before {
  content: "";
  inline-size: 1em;
  block-size: 1em;
  flex: none;
  -webkit-mask: ${AI_ICON_MASK};
  mask: ${AI_ICON_MASK};
}
`;

export const button: Definition = defineComponent({
  name: "button",
  css: (p) => appendGenerated(buttonRaw.replaceAll(SENTINEL, p), interpolatedRules(p)),
});

export const buttonCss: Definition["css"] = button.css;
```

The button CSS file uses `@scope` with nested selectors for modifiers like `-color-primary`, `-size-sm`, `-size-md`, `-size-lg`, `-shape-circle`, `-shape-square`, `-toggle`, `-without-background`, `-on-color`, etc.

---

## 2. **Existing Group/Composite Component: `radio-input-group`**

[radio-input-group](formats/components/src/components/radio-input-group/index.ts) is a perfect group-style component example:

```ts
import { defineComponent, type Definition } from "../../lib/define.ts";
import { SENTINEL } from "../../lib/sentinel.ts";
import { radioInputGroup as radioInputGroupRaw } from "../../generated/component-styles.ts";

export const radioInputGroup: Definition = defineComponent({
  name: "radio-input-group",
  css: (p) => radioInputGroupRaw.replaceAll(SENTINEL, p),
});
export const radioInputGroupCss: Definition["css"] = radioInputGroup.css;
```

[radio-input-group CSS](formats/components/src/components/radio-input-group/radio-input-group.css) shows nested child scoping:

```css
@scope (.pfx-radio-input-group) {
  & {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--instui-component-form-field-layout-gap-inputs);
  }

  & > legend {
    padding: 0;
    margin-block-end: var(--instui-component-form-field-layout-gap-primitives);
  }

  &.-required > legend::after {
    content: "*";
    margin-inline-start: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--instui-component-form-field-layout-asterisk-color);
  }

  /* Child layout variants */
  &.-layout-columns,
  &.-layout-inline {
    flex-flow: row wrap;
    align-items: center;
    column-gap: var(--instui-spacing-space-md);
  }

  &.-layout-columns > legend,
  &.-layout-inline > legend {
    flex-basis: 100%;
  }

  &.-variant-toggle {
    flex-flow: row wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0;
  }

  &.-variant-toggle > .pfx-radio:has(input:focus-visible) {
    z-index: 1;
  }
}
```

Other group-style components: `toggle-group`, `form-field-group`, `drawer-layout`, `table` (with members).

---

## 3. **Helper Functions & Signatures**

From [define.ts](formats/components/src/lib/define.ts):

```ts
export interface Definition {
  name: string;
  kind: CssRecordKind; // "component" | "utility" | "rule" | "declaration"
  rules(this: void, prefix: string, options?: ComponentOptions): string;
  css(this: void, options?: ComponentOptions): string;
}

export interface DefineInput {
  name: string;
  css: (p: string, options?: ComponentOptions) => string;
}

export const defineComponent = (input: DefineInput): Definition => make("component", input);
export const defineUtility = (input: DefineInput): Definition => make("utility", input);
export const defineRule = (input: DefineInput): Definition => make("rule", input);
export const defineDeclaration = (input: DefineInput): Definition => make("declaration", input);
```

From [helpers.ts](formats/components/src/lib/helpers.ts):

```ts
export interface ComponentOptions {
  prefix?: string | null; // "instui" → ".instui-button"; falsy → ".button"
  theme?: ComponentTheme; // "rebrand" | "canvas" | "canvasHighContrast"
}

export const ns = (prefix: string | null | undefined): string => 
  (prefix ? `${prefix}-` : "");
```

---

## 4. **@scope Usage with Nested Child Selectors**

Toggle-group is a perfect example with nested child scoping:

```css
@scope (.pfx-toggle-group) {
  & {
    display: block;
    border: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid var(--instui-component-toggle-group-border-color);
    border-radius: var(--instui-border-radius-md);
  }

  /* Direct child selectors for nested elements */
  & > summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-icon-margin);
    cursor: pointer;
    list-style: none;
    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-medium);
  }

  & > summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  & > summary::before {
    content: "";
    flex: none;
    inline-size: 1em;
    block-size: 1em;
    background: currentColor;
    -webkit-mask: var(--instui-icon-chevron-right) center / contain no-repeat;
    mask: var(--instui-icon-chevron-right) center / contain no-repeat;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  &[open] > summary::before {
    transform: rotate(90deg);
  }

  /* Non-summary children separated by top border */
  & > :not(summary) {
    border-block-start: var(--instui-border-width-sm) solid
      var(--instui-component-toggle-group-border-color);
    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-medium);
  }

  /* Size modifiers affect nested elements */
  &.-size-sm > summary,
  &.-size-sm > :not(summary) {
    font-size: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-font-size-small);
    padding: var(--instui-component-toggle-details-content-padding-small);
  }

  &.-without-border {
    border: 0;
  }

  &.-without-border > :not(summary) {
    border-block-start: 0;
  }
}
```

Key patterns:
- `& > child` — direct children
- `& > :not(summary)` — negation selectors
- `& > summary::before` — pseudo-elements on children
- `&[state] > child` — state-based child styling
- `&.-modifier > child` — modifier affecting children

---

## 5. **Registry Pattern: `index.ts` Files**

[components/index.ts](formats/components/src/components/index.ts) is the **barrel + registry** (load-bearing order):

```ts
// Order MUST match componentsCss() concat order (NOT alphabetical)
export const COMPONENTS: readonly Definition[] = [
  button,
  alert,
  badge,
  pill,
  tag,
  avatar,
  tabs,
  tabsTab,
  tabsPanel,
  // ... more components in concat order
  toggleGroup,
  // ... etc
];
```

From [define.ts](formats/components/src/lib/define.ts), the `rules()` method concatenates them:

```ts
const rules = (prefix: string, options: ComponentOptions = {}): string => {
  const { comment, body } = splitLeadingDocComment(cssBuilder(prefix, options));
  const docs = withSizeAliasDocs(comment, body);
  return `${docs}\n${withAliases(withSizeAliases(body), aliasPairs).trim()}\n`;
};
```

**To add a new component:**
1. Create `src/components/<name>/<name>.css` + `src/components/<name>/index.ts`
2. Import and add to `COMPONENTS` array in the exact position it should concat
3. Export `<name>Css` from `src/index.ts`
4. Add to `tests/public-surface.test.ts`'s `EXPECTED` list

---

## 6. **Test File Pattern: Drift-Checked Tests**

[alert.test.ts](formats/components/tests/components/alert.test.ts) shows the pattern:

```ts
import { expect, test } from "vite-plus/test";
import { alertCss } from "../../src/index.ts";
import { alert } from "../../src/components/alert/index.ts";
import { validate } from "../_validate.ts"; // The drift-check helper

// Drift-check: validates CSS parses to one record, name/kind match, & no unknown tokens
test("alert: emits exactly one well-formed cssdoc record with no token drift", () => {
  validate(alert);
});

// Behavior tests: verify CSS output contains expected rules/modifiers
test("alert supports token-backed floating and inline status treatments", () => {
  const css = alertCss({ prefix: "instui" });
  expect(css).toContain("&:is(.-variant-success, .-color-success)");
  expect(css).toContain("&:is(.-variant-warning, .-color-warning)");
  expect(css).toContain("&:is(.-variant-error, .-color-danger, .-color-error)");
  // Verify token references exist
  for (const status of ["info", "success", "warning", "danger"]) {
    expect(css).toContain(`--instui-component-alert-${status}-background`);
  }
  // Verify modifiers, pseudo-elements, aliases exist
  expect(css).toContain("&::after");
  expect(css).toContain('&[class*="-icon-"]::before');
  expect(css).toContain("content: none");
  // Verify child patterns (e.g., button-group)
  expect(css).toContain("& > .button-group");
  expect(css).toContain(".button-group > .instui-button");
});
```

The [_validate.ts](formats/components/tests/_validate.ts) helper:

```ts
export function validate(def: Definition): void {
  const css = def.css({ prefix: "instui", theme: "rebrand" });
  const entries = parseCssDocs(css, { configuration });
  if (entries.length !== 1)
    throw new Error(`${def.name}: expected exactly one cssdoc record, got ${entries.length}`);
  const [entry] = entries;
  if (entry.kind !== def.kind)
    throw new Error(`${def.name}: parsed kind "${entry.kind}" ≠ declared "${def.kind}"`);
  if (entry.name !== def.name)
    throw new Error(`${def.name}: parsed name "${entry.name}" ≠ declared "${def.name}"`);
  // Check each theme for unknown token drift
  for (const theme of ["rebrand", "canvas", "canvasHighContrast"] as const) {
    const themedCss = def.css({ prefix: "instui", theme });
    const drift = unknownReferences(themedCss, byTheme(theme)).filter((r) => !isLocal(r));
    if (drift.length)
      throw new Error(`${def.name} (${theme}): unknown token reference(s): ${drift.join(", ")}`);
  }
}
```

---

## 7. **Demo File Structure**

Demos are **generated from cssdoc `@demo` tags**, not separate markdown files. The alert component doc block has:

```ts
/**
 * @component alert
 * @summary A status message with floating and inline surface treatments and a masked status glyph from the shared icon set.
 * @remarks ...
 * @example -nocard
 * ```html
 * <div class="pfx-alert -icon-megaphone --mb-md">
 *   An alert with the default info color, and a custom icon.
 * </div>
 * <div class="pfx-alert -color-success --mb-md">
 *   Congratulations! You're using the "success" color.
 *     <button class="pfx-button">Ok</button>
 *   <button class="pfx-close-button" aria-label="Close"></button>
 * </div>
 * ```
 * @structure
 * .pfx-alert {
 *   slot {}
 *   @variant bare-button { @component button:max-1 {} }
 *   @variant button-group { .button-group { @component button:one-or-more:max-2 {} } }
 *   @component close-button:optional {}
 * }
 * @related close-button — The dismiss control an alert may include.
 * @demo self:alert
 */
```

Demos are **embedded in the component's own CSS file** as cssdoc metadata (not separate files).

---

## 8. **Guide Markdown Structure**

Guides are hand-authored markdown in [docs/guide/](docs/guide/) (not auto-generated). Existing guides:
- [docs/guide/getting-started.md](docs/guide/getting-started.md)
- [docs/guide/cdn-picker.md](docs/guide/cdn-picker.md)
- [docs/guide/plugins.md](docs/guide/plugins.md)

API documentation is generated from cssdoc in the CSS files themselves (not separate guide files). The cssdoc `@component`, `@modifier`, `@example`, `@structure` tags generate the API pages automatically.

---

## 9. **Modifier Convention Documentation**

From [docs/conventions/authoring.md](docs/conventions/authoring.md):

**RSCSS Key-Value Compounds:**
- `.${p}<comp>.-<prop>-<val>` aligned to InstUI prop names
- Examples: `-color-secondary`, `-size-sm`, `-shape-circle`, `-variant-toggle`

**Booleans:**
- Presence = true (e.g., `-clickable`, `-condensed`)
- Default-on booleans inverted: `-without-background`, `-without-border`, `-without-shadow`

**Sizes (one shared scale):**
- `-size-{xs,sm,md,lg,xl}` with both short and long spellings via `withSizeAliases()`
- Long forms: `-size-small`, `-size-medium`, `-size-large`, etc.

**Nested elements:**
- Unprefixed short classes scoped as descendants: `.instui-menu .item` (not BEM `__`)
- Flat prefixed non-nested parts: `.instui-badge-wrapper`

**Global utilities (double-dash namespace):**
- `--bg-secondary`, `--margin-bottom-small`, `--gap-md` (never single-dash)
- Chainable onto any component: `<button class="instui-button --bg-danger">`

**Deprecated/Alias modifiers (auto-discovered):**
- `@alias {@link -canonical}` — pure rename (functional twin)
- `@deprecated {@link -canonical}` — true deprecation (behavior changed, still works)

From [README.md](formats/components/README.md):

> An InstUI-look CSS component library, built from the `--instui-*` tokens... `components.css` — class-based component styles (`<button class="instui-button">`)... `utilities.css` — opt-in cross-cutting classes: spacing, layout, and semantic color/token utilities.

---

## 10. **Package Scripts for `formats/components`**

From [package.json](formats/components/package.json):

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "component-styles": "node scripts/component-styles.ts",
    "dev": "vp run @pantoken/plugin-theme-custom-media#build && node scripts/component-styles.ts && node scripts/generate.ts && node scripts/build-entries.ts && vp pack --watch",
    "test": "vp run @pantoken/plugin-theme-custom-media#build && node scripts/component-styles.ts && vp test",
    "check": "vp run @pantoken/plugin-theme-custom-media#build && node scripts/component-styles.ts && node scripts/build-entries.ts && vp check"
  }
}
```

**Usage:**
- `vp test` — Run tests (includes `component-styles` build)
- `vp check` — Format, lint, type-check (includes `component-styles` + `build-entries`)
- `vp check --fix` — Auto-fix formatting/imports
- `vp run check:publish` — (from root) validates publishability

The `component-styles` script generates the IR from `.css` files.

---

## **CSS Tag Gotchas**

From [css.ts](formats/components/src/lib/css.ts):

```ts
/**
 * The `css` tagged-template — an identity tag that just returns the interpolated string.
 * Authoring with the `css` tag lets cssdoc's scanner recognize it as an embedded stylesheet,
 * so the editor and any `.ts`-level lint read the CSS (selectors and all), not just the doc comment.
 */
export const css = (strings: TemplateStringsArray, ...values: readonly unknown[]): string =>
  strings.reduce((out, chunk, i) => out + (i ? String(values[i - 1]) : "") + chunk, "");
```

**Critical:**
1. **Tag every CSS body with `css`** — enables editor syntax highlighting and linting
2. **Add `// prettier-ignore` right before the template** — oxfmt corrupts interpolated selectors (`${p}foo.-mod` → `${p}foo .-mod`, wrong meaning)
3. Never use escaped backticks or `${` inside doc comments — `*/` substring in prose truncates the comment silently (see JS-TS gotchas note on regex/glob literals)
4. Use `@scope (.pfx-<name>) { & { ... } }` pattern — keeps ownership explicit, reduces duplication, produces stable diffs

---

## **Aliases & Size Twins**

From [aliases.ts](formats/components/src/lib/aliases.ts):

```ts
// appendGenerated() — append rules INSIDE trailing @scope block (not after it)
// Needed when you have interpolated rules to add after the base .css-authored record
export function appendGenerated(css: string, extra: string): string { ... }

// withSizeAliases() — auto-emit long spellings (-size-small for -size-sm)
// withAliases() — auto-emit @alias/@deprecated twins from doc comments
// deprecatedAliasPairs() — parse @modifier -alias — @alias/@deprecated {@link -canonical}
```

**Workflow:**
1. Author component in `.css` file with cssdoc metadata
2. `defineComponent({ name, css: (p) => ... })` calls `withSizeAliases()` + `withAliases()`
3. Auto-generated twins append to the body (before the doc comment is added)
4. Tests validate the record via `validate(def)` (drift-checks all 3 themes)

